## What I Learned
How to use the pipe operator to chain commands together. 
Instead of saving the server output to a file and then 
searching it, piping sends the output of one command 
directly into another in real time. This is a fundamental 
Linux skill used constantly in security work — filtering 
live log output, searching command results, and chaining 
multiple filters together to narrow down exactly what 
you are looking for.
